    "narrative": "Our primary target today is **Jose Caballero**, who sits at an elite 80.26, fueled by a significant +13% platoon edge against Corbin. In a league where stolen bases remain the scarcest commodity, **Jose Caballero** is our most vital asset. He is joined in the top tier by **Corbin Carroll** (78.36), who despite a slight dynamic platoon disadvantage against Abbott, benefits from a favorable 4.72 xERA matchup. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Josh Naylor** also project strongly today, both surpassing the 72.0 threshold as they capitalize on high-xERA matchups against Sugano and Poulin, respectively. These four players anchor our lineup, providing the high-floor production needed to sustain our Roto standing.\n\nThe tightest decision at the margins involved **Kyle Karros**, who narrowly edged out bench considerations with a 54.01 projection. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from a +7% platoon boost against Springs, his lower batting order position anchors his efficiency. We remain cautious with **Seiya Suzuki** (45.46) and **Austin Riley** (52.68), both of whom are facing elite arms in Webb and Peralta. Their scores reflect the reality of pitching-heavy matchups; however, they remain locked in because our depth options\u2014including **Brice Turang**, who is currently out of the starting lineup\u2014are unavailable to provide a superior alternative. We are closely monitoring weather reports regarding the wind-aided park factor for **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, which added a slight +5% boost to their otherwise marginal scores against Hudson. Given our current game cap strategy, we are leaning into the high-upside speed profiles of **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll** to navigate today's slate.",
